Checking StyleBro's rules and the built-in rules init and migrate turn on (141 ids), changing nothing; --all checks every analyzer's and compiler fix too.
Visual Basic: Client_VB.vbproj, Server_VB.vbproj, Shared_VB.vbproj: Visual Basic projects are left alone, 'format' runs on the C# projects only.
Held back: IDE0049: this .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' ignores the suppressor StyleBro's multi-target guard uses for IDE rules, so their fixes could write C# or APIs that another target framework or project compiling the same file doesn't have. They aren't applied here; a newer .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' applies them where the guard allows.
Multi-targeted: one 'dotnet format' run per target framework (net10.0, net10.0-windows, net472, net8.0, netstandard2.0, netstandard2.1). net8.0, netstandard2.1: only the projects whose code compiles differently there.
Configurations: runs for Release (Client, DN_Client, docs, JustProtos and 12 more) too: their code compiles differently there ('#if DEBUG', files or docs of that configuration), and the build of every configuration gets the same fixes and checks.
Shared files: these projects compile the same files with other '#if' symbols or settings, so each group gets a run of its own (loaded together, 'dotnet format' crashes: https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/issues/86001): protobuf-net.Grpc.Test.Integration | protobuf-net.Grpc.Test.IntegrationUpLevel.
